A core that traps after another core took regions from its thread's process does not load them again as it takes the lock,
so the trap runs, and the self-check reads the protection unit, with regions the process no longer has.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2 smp-test
Report: the core's regions wait to be loaded again

diff --git a/kernel/core.c b/kernel/core.c
--- a/kernel/core.c
+++ b/kernel/core.c
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@ void core_enter(void)
      * unless the thread lost its process too, or went, and the next switch loads another process's.
      */
     const struct thread *t = core->current;
-    if (core->pmp_stale && t != NULL && thread_process(t) != NULL) {
+    if (false && t != NULL && thread_process(t) != NULL) {
         core->pmp_stale = false;
         process_activate(thread_process(t));
     }
